From cf267eb667616964fa3ef79f5c2641d80cc1f0f2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <claude@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 23 Aug 2026 09:41:28 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Reliability plan (Phase 7): file outbox + Hangfire memory
 storage + 30-minute sweep + startup scan

Rebuilt against the actual current repo state (commit 2a0a577) after the
previous version of this patch was generated against an out-of-date
Program.cs/appsettings.json that predated the 401-fix patch's changes -
that mismatch is what caused the earlier apply failures, not an issue
with the two patches being incompatible with each other. Content is
otherwise identical to what was described previously:

- Outbox/OutboxStore.cs: OutboxEntry + IOutboxStore/FileOutboxStore, one
  JSON file per pending entry under a configurable directory
  (Outbox:Directory), keyed by idempotency key.
- Outbox/OutboxReconciliationJob.cs: sweeps every pending entry, retries
  RecordPrintResultAsync, deletes on success, records attempt
  count/last failure and re-queues on failure.
- MachineController.Print: the existing 207 branch now also writes an
  outbox entry before returning, carrying the original bearer token.
- Program.cs: IOutboxStore (singleton)/OutboxReconciliationJob (scoped)
  registered; AddHangfire(UseMemoryStorage())/AddHangfireServer() wired
  in; startup scan runs once before the app starts serving, then
  RecurringJob.AddOrUpdate schedules the same job every 30 minutes via
  Cron.MinuteInterval(30). Main is now async Task; app.Run() ->
  await app.RunAsync().
- invetoryBackGroundServices.csproj: Hangfire.AspNetCore 1.8.14 and
  Hangfire.MemoryStorage 1.8.1.1 added.

Same unresolved limitation as before, still open: every OutboxEntry
carries a Print Agent token with a 5-minute default lifetime, while the
reconciliation sweep runs every 30 minutes - by the time a scheduled
sweep fires, that token will essentially always be expired, and the
Printer Agent cannot mint itself a new one. The startup scan has a real
chance of working; the scheduled sweep will typically just log the
expired token and re-queue. See OutboxReconciliationJob's doc comment
for the three resolution paths - still your call, not picked here.

No dotnet SDK or NuGet access in the authoring environment. Verified by
re-reading the actual current Program.cs/appsettings.json/
MachineController.cs/csproj directly from this exact commit before
making any edit (not assumed from a prior session), the full-repo
symbol-table cross-check (same four already-known false positives,
nothing new), brace balance across every touched file, and JSON/XML
validity on appsettings.json, the .csproj, and both resx files.
